1
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for a certain day
drifting on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble,
even my shoes go flying.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,900
Onto the head of the carpenter
I was putting in a choke hold,

4
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
pachinko, a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,240
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the setting sun falls toward the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it ends just like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika, Shibamata,
again, even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,540
Because I'm a fool who only
realized after hearing it.

13
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,280
Up Close! The Dangerous Duo!

14
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:44,540
Did you see that, Nakagawa?

15
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:48,700
Bonded perfectly in 0.4 seconds.
Impressive, isn't it?

16
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:50,100
I see.

17
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:53,600
It's all thanks to Super Cement X.

18
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:59,760
This adhesive is so strong it's banned from sale in Japan.
It's a marvel.

19
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,860
That's why I had it shipped
from America by mail order.

20
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:04,620
It cost 30,000 yen a tube!

21
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:08,880
It sticks to any material, no matter how difficult.
Anything goes.

22
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:12,720
Just a tiny dab like this,
and even something this heavy

23
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,400
stays put. Just like that!

24
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,980
W-wow, that's amazing.

25
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:21,260
It's so strong it's scary.

26
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,460
So that's why it's only
available by mail order.

27
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:27,420
What if you apply it by mistake?

28
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,560
Well, a neutralizer
comes included in the set.

29
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,080
Without it,
things could get seriously out of hand.

30
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,840
It really is made for modelers, isn't it.

31
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,220
Kei-chan, come here for a sec.

32
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,460
Yes, excuse me.

33
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,280
The work's going smoothly,
and there's hardly any spillover,

34
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,380
Super Cement X really is a lifesaver.

35
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:52,600
Wh-what's going on?

36
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:54,260
Idiot, you're stuck together!

37
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:56,740
Hey, don't kill the Super X!

38
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:57,920
You idiot!

39
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,020
Ow

40
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:02,940
Let go, let go, let go!

41
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,740
Help me, Nakagawa!

42
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,320
Help!

43
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,580
Senpai, what on earth happened?

44
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:13,440
Nakagawa, quick,
use the neutralizer to get this off me!

45
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,860
I-I thought the top of the
kotatsu had a kotatsu too!

46
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:20,180
I-I-I-I-I-I-I-I!

47
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,760
Please separate slowly.

48
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:25,440
The neutralizer is slowly running out.

49
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,580
Idiot, use it carefully!

50
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,620
What on earth is this commotion?

51
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,920
Chief, we spilled the
super-strong adhesive...

52
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:35,260
Apparently our bodies
got stuck to the kotatsu.

53
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:38,320
Honestly, you're always up to this
kind of nonsense all year round.

54
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,320
If you just peel it off all at once,
it'll come off, right?

55
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,840
My flesh is coming off!

56
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:47,020
You have to peel it off little by little with the neutralizer,
or it won't work.

57
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:51,260
Wouldn't it be better to just leave them like this for a while?
Then they wouldn't have to go out and slack off.

58
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,500
Finally, I'm a free man again.

59
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,460
Alright, now I'll take the bottle off.

60
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:00,900
Mm.

61
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,080
Just a little more.

62
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:09,820
Ow

63
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,440
It hurts

64
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,420
It's Super Cement X!

65
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:15,920
Chief!

66
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:16,760
What is it?!

67
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:19,200
If you go down, we'll stick together!

68
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,900
What the hell, you idiot!
Hurry up and do something!

69
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:24,380
Don't say that to me!

70
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,480
Super Cement X!

71
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,880
Thank goodness. For a while there,
I didn't know what would happen.

72
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:49,700
What did you say?

73
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,720
Let go of me, you creep!

74
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:55,340
No, Chief, that's -

75
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,020
I'd like to talk, but -

76
00:04:57,020 --> 00:05:00,200
It seems that adhesive stuck to us -

77
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,320
Idiot! Get it off, quick!

78
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,840
I know, I know.

79
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:08,260
Hey, Nakagawa, the neutralizer!

80
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,020
Well, you see...

81
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,680
Ow ow, Chief!

82
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,860
It's impossible, right, Chief?

83
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,800
Ow, I told you it's impossible!

84
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,220
You idiot!

85
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,460
We've got a squad leaders'
meeting this afternoon!

86
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,100
What do you think you're doing?

87
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,620
Now, now, Chief.

88
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:32,620
Senpai,

89
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:37,480
Don't you have any other modeler
friends who have Super Cement X?

90
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,320
Nice one, Nakagawa!

91
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,840
Can this be fixed?

92
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:43,800
Yes that guy, I think he's

93
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:46,440
Sorry, Chief,

94
00:05:46,490 --> 00:05:50,460
he's gone to Tibet to train for
something he's been thinking about.

95
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:53,080
You idiot, getting my hopes up!

96
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,120
Chief, there's no point
in fighting like this.

97
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,560
Nakagawa, can't you do something?

98
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:01,400
Even if you say that,
there's nothing I can do.

99
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,900
Do something, Nakagawa!

100
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:06,320
This happened because you spilled the neutralizer,
you know!

101
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,600
That's because you bumped into me, senpai.

102
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:14,400
No, you should have been careful and
peeled the Super Cement X off my hand.

103
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,720
It's because you yanked it off by force.

104
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:18,080
Besides, it was your fault for
not putting the lid on properly.

105
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,960
It's because you kept saying
"Wow, that's amazing!" and stuff.

106
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,220
I got carried away showing it off too,
and then the cat attacked me.

107
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,460
That cat only came around
because you kept feeding it.

108
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:27,480
Isn't that why it started
coming to the police box?

109
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,160
Spoiled rich kids like you are such a pain.

110
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,560
If you feel bad about it, fix it right now.

111
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,880
Hey, are you listening?

112
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,120
What do you think you're doing?

113
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:38,700
Sets in 0.4 seconds!

114
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,240
Idiot, we don't have a choice. Let's go!

115
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:49,100
Since it's come to this, you're coming
to the squad leaders' meeting too.

116
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,420
Why me too?

117
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:53,440
Chief, are you really
going to the show like this?

118
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,520
I refuse to walk around town like this.

119
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,840
We can't skip it. It's important.

120
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,320
Anyway, I refuse.

121
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:05,020
Right, what if we pretend it's a prisoner
transfer and drape a handkerchief over them?

122
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:09,700
Reiko, that's rude!
That makes the chief look like the criminal!

123
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:13,000
Idiot, anyone can see you
look more like the criminal!

124
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:17,060
Then how about carrying
this old refrigerator?

125
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,480
Well, it's a somewhat natural style,
I suppose.

126
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:24,720
Seriously?

127
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:29,220
I'm leaving, so the rest is up to you.
Be careful, okay?

128
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:36,780
Don't be angry, Kei-chan.
Want some rice crackers?

129
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:49,600
Why do we have to carry something this heavy?
Whose fault do you think this is?

130
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,900
Chief, wait, stop!

131
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,760
What? We don't have time!

132
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:59,860
I really need to pee.

133
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,260
Just hold it in.

134
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:06,320
No way.
I'll go do it in the empty lot out back.

135
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,680
You idiot! Police officers
don't go taking a leak in public!

136
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,400
Fine, we'll take a short break.

137
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,580
Welcome!

138
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,700
Excuse me, could you lend us your restroom?

139
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:26,180
It's in the back.

140
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:27,860
Chief, hurry!

141
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:32,400
Take your time.

142
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,460
Here it is! Chief, hurry, hurry!

143
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,620
Wait a moment, Ryotsu!

144
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,400
What is it already?

145
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:43,740
Two men going into the restroom together?
People will get the wrong idea!

146
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,200
No way, we're stuck together!

147
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:53,080
Whoa, I'm gonna leak!

148
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:55,880
Ryotsu, wait!

149
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,120
I'm leaking, I'm leaking!

150
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,700
My social standing is...

151
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,840
What are you doing, you idiot?

152
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,740
Don't put your hand there!

153
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:09,140
You have to unzip it and pull it out,
or it won't work!

154
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:12,420
Now I have to touch your filthy thing too!

155
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,880
What do you want me to do?
We came all the way here!

156
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,780
You're the one who invited me, Chief.

157
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:19,160
I didn't invite you. I just...

158
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:21,780
If we've come this far,
that means you're fine with it too, right?

159
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:26,100
Fine, fine. Just stop shouting so loudly.

160
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:29,060
Pull your pants and underwear
down together and do your business.

161
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,720
Are you done yet?

162
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:43,360
Yes.

163
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:44,920
Chief.

164
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,351
Doing it in a situation like this,

165
00:09:49,401 --> 00:09:51,940
it's oddly thrilling,
in a guilty sort of way.

166
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,440
W-what are you, an idiot?
Just hurry up already.

167
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:55,780
This is bad.

168
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,600
What now?

169
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:59,660
I also need to take a big dump now.

170
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,960
Idiot, hold it in!

171
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:04,020
Because we're already almost to the exit.

172
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:04,980
Shut up.

173
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,660
Don't pull so hard.
The jolt's going to make me go.

174
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:08,760
I'm gonna go, I'm gonna go.

175
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,680
Let's go, Ryotsu.

176
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,240
Chief!

177
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:16,000
Chief, wait.
Just a little more, just a little more.

178
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,160
W-wait, you forgot the fridge.

179
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:21,300
Y-yeah, whatever. I'm too tired to carry it to the station.
I'm leaving it behind.

180
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,206
No, wait, Chief.

181
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:25,540
I still haven't put my pants on! Chief!

182
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:37,380
Without carrying something,
we'd really stand out

183
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:44,540
Well, two middle-aged men holding
hands while walking look 100% weird.

184
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:48,840
If we walk while dancing like this,
it won't look unnatural.

185
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,760
There, it's quick-quick-slow!

186
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:53,060
Quick-quick-slow, Chief.

187
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:54,560
It's not unnatural at all.

188
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,200
That'll make us stand out even more,
you idiot.

189
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:00,800
I just got punched by my own hand.

190
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,120
Ryo-san.

191
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,320
We've been looking for you, Ryo-san.

192
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:08,100
Everyone's been waiting at Jansō since noon.

193
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,420
Why didn't you show up, of all days today?

194
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:13,140
What are you babbling about?

195
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,000
I'm not going to die.

196
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,660
What?

197
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:19,380
You're not trying to wipe out all of yesterday's losses like that,
are you?

198
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:20,620
Fine.

199
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:22,360
Come on, it's not like you invited me.

200
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,240
Being together like this,

201
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:30,160
I can clearly see what you're up to.

202
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:31,760
You must have mistaken me for someone else.

203
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,440
Really, really.

204
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,460
Telling such an obvious lie.

205
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:38,020
Ow, what are you doing?
My joint's coming off!

206
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,420
This way,
I won't have to look at your annoying face.

207
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:43,920
Damn that chief.

208
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:49,380
Damn it,
today was the release day for Kue Kue!

209
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,720
Me of all people...

210
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,160
Hey, where do you think you're going?

211
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,900
Chief, excuse me for a moment.

212
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:57,580
Today was the release day for Kue Kue,
you know.

213
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,580
What's this "Kure Kure" thing?

214
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:02,780
It's not "Kure Kure," it's "Kue Kue."

215
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:06,460
That doesn't matter. We'll be late for the squad leaders' meeting,
so do it later.

216
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:09,620
It's a popular software,
so it'll sell out in no time.

217
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,680
Shut up!

218
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,920
Move! Ryotsu, move!

219
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,640
Move how?

220
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,340
Gah! Hey, it hurts! It really hurts!

221
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,880
It hurts, it hurts, Ryotsu.

222
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:27,880
Say that again. Even if you say that,
it hurts, hurts, hurts.

223
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:31,820
Well, it's because Chief

224
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,780
Speaking of you, it's you who

225
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:36,460
But we ended up in this position

226
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:36,920
Chief

227
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,020
Honey

228
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,620
Why did it turn out like this?

229
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:51,580
That's my line, dammit!

230
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:14,940
Thanks to you, I've had a terrible time.

231
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:18,080
Well, we made it in time,
so what's the problem?

232
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:21,240
So you're saying it's fine to dress
like this as long as we're on time?

233
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,280
Make sure you keep quiet during
the squad leaders' meeting.

234
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:26,140
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

235
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:29,800
That Chief, always going on about hitting us.
Just you wait!

236
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:36,220
Ohara-kun, what's going on here?

237
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:40,380
Well, Ryotsu here has wanted
to study this for a while.

238
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:43,560
He really wants to listen in
on the squad leaders' meeting.

239
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:46,280
No, I understand Ryotsu's enthusiasm, but -

240
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,760
What we're talking about is that outfit.

241
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:54,440
When did you end up dressed like this...
Right, Ryotsu?

242
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:04,840
Now, regarding the serial purse-snatchings
happening throughout the city,

243
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:10,100
based on the victims' and witnesses' testimonies,
it's highly likely they're the same culprit.

244
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,560
Hey, wake up, hey!

245
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,540
So,

246
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,860
What's the matter, Ryotsu?

247
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:21,260
Sorry, I got a bit nervous.

248
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:28,260
Damn the Chief,
making us attend this pointless meeting,

249
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:30,980
and on top of that,
he didn't have to headbutt us, did he?

250
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:32,580
Yeah, that's right!

251
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,760
What is it, Chief?
Suddenly taking my hand like this?

252
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:46,140
Daijiro-chan, you just don't
